1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,205
Ava: If your PyTorch workload has to run across a large GPU cluster, the framework is only part of the story.
Ava：如果你的 PyTorch 工作负载需要在大型 GPU 集群上运行，框架只是其中一环。

2
00:00:07,205 --> 00:00:11,361
Scheduling work and operating the infrastructure matter too.
任务调度和基础设施运维也很重要。

3
00:00:11,361 --> 00:00:19,262
Nscale has joined the PyTorch Foundation as a Platinum member, so this announcement touches all three layers.
Nscale 已作为白金会员加入 PyTorch 基金会，因此这则消息涉及这三个层面。

4
00:00:19,262 --> 00:00:26,179
Brian: And it matters because Nscale is also tied to Ray, which sits in the Foundation's project ecosystem.
Brian：这很重要，因为 Nscale 也与 Ray 有关联，而 Ray 属于基金会的项目生态。

5
00:00:26,179 --> 00:00:30,398
Nscale says it'll keep investing in Ray and its contributors.
Nscale 表示将继续投入 Ray 及其贡献者社区。

6
00:00:30,398 --> 00:00:40,708
The immediate news is organizational, but the engineering question is how PyTorch, distributed computing, and cloud infrastructure fit together.
眼前是组织层面的消息，但工程上的问题是 PyTorch、分布式计算和云基础设施如何协同。

7
00:00:40,708 --> 00:00:42,329
Ava: Let's put that in context.
Ava：我们来看看背景。

8
00:00:42,329 --> 00:00:49,621
A training loop can be clear and efficient on one machine, while a much larger run depends on work outside that loop.
训练循环在单机上可能清晰高效，但大规模运行还依赖循环之外的工作。

9
00:00:49,621 --> 00:00:58,386
The announcement seems to be asking whether the framework, the distributed layer, and the cluster can work together with less friction.
这则公告似乎在探讨，框架、分布式层和集群能否更顺畅地协同。

10
00:00:58,386 --> 00:01:05,006
Brian: That's the stated direction. Nscale describes itself as a full-stack AI cloud platform.
Brian：这是其宣称的方向。Nscale 将自己定位为全栈 AI 云平台。

11
00:01:05,006 --> 00:01:12,083
It brings power, data centers, compute, and software into one vertically integrated offering.
它将电力、数据中心、算力和软件整合为一体化服务。

12
00:01:12,083 --> 00:01:16,496
Its cloud platform is meant for AI training and inference.
其云平台面向 AI 训练和推理。

13
00:01:16,496 --> 00:01:25,064
That description tells us what parts of the stack Nscale operates; it doesn't specify a new PyTorch feature.
这种描述说明了 Nscale 运营技术栈中的哪些部分，并未指出 PyTorch 的新功能。

14
00:01:25,064 --> 00:01:30,439
Ava: Suppose a team wants to take an existing model workload beyond one machine.
Ava：假设一个团队想把现有模型工作负载扩展到单机之外。

15
00:01:30,439 --> 00:01:36,531
I can see why the handoff between layers would matter. The model code is one concern.
我能理解各层之间的衔接为何重要。模型代码是一方面。

16
00:01:36,531 --> 00:01:39,111
Getting work distributed is another.
如何分配任务是另一方面。

17
00:01:39,111 --> 00:01:43,339
Then someone has to provide and run the underlying cluster.
还得有人提供并运行底层集群。

18
00:01:43,339 --> 00:01:46,126
Where does Ray enter that picture?
Ray 在其中扮演什么角色？

19
00:01:46,126 --> 00:01:52,729
Brian: The article calls Ray an open-source framework for distributed computing and scaling AI workloads.
Brian：文章称 Ray 是用于分布式计算和扩展 AI 工作负载的开源框架。

20
00:01:52,729 --> 00:02:08,844
Nick Jones, Nscale's vice president of cloud native platform engineering, draws a broad distinction: PyTorch keeps the Pythonic style researchers know while addressing performance, and Ray helps that work run across thousands of GPUs.
Nscale 云原生平台工程副总裁 Nick Jones 作了概括性区分：PyTorch 在提升性能的同时保留研究人员熟悉的 Python 风格，而 Ray 帮助这些工作在数千张 GPU 上运行。

21
00:02:08,844 --> 00:02:10,699
Ava: That's a useful distinction.
Ava：这个区分很有帮助。

22
00:02:10,699 --> 00:02:18,055
Ray addresses the problem of distributing AI work, while Nscale is talking about the infrastructure beneath it.
Ray 解决 AI 工作的分布式运行问题，而 Nscale 关注其底层基础设施。

23
00:02:18,055 --> 00:02:26,140
For our hypothetical team, those are separate engineering decisions: how to spread the work, and what cluster will run it.
对我们假设的团队来说，这是两个不同的工程决策：如何分配任务，以及由什么集群运行任务。

24
00:02:26,140 --> 00:02:33,050
The announcement connects the layers as an ambition rather than describing a particular job design.
这则公告把这些层面的衔接作为目标，并未描述具体的作业设计。

25
00:02:33,050 --> 00:02:35,958
Brian: The link to Ray also needs careful wording.
Brian：与 Ray 的关联也需要说准确。

26
00:02:35,958 --> 00:02:40,625
Nscale has a planned acquisition of Anyscale, the company behind Ray.
Nscale 计划收购 Ray 背后的公司 Anyscale。

27
00:02:40,625 --> 00:02:47,998
The article says Nscale has committed to continued investment in Ray's development and contributor community.
文章称 Nscale 已承诺继续投资 Ray 的开发及其贡献者社区。

28
00:02:47,998 --> 00:02:55,720
The acquisition is described as planned, so we should keep that future step separate from today's membership.
收购仍处于计划阶段，因此要与今天的入会分开看。

29
00:02:55,720 --> 00:02:59,219
Ava: What does that change for Ray's position in the Foundation?
Ava：这会怎样影响 Ray 在基金会中的地位？

30
00:02:59,219 --> 00:03:06,334
If a cloud provider is investing in a distributed framework, I'd want to know how that relates to the project community.
如果一家云服务商投资分布式框架，我会想知道这与项目社区有什么关系。

31
00:03:06,334 --> 00:03:14,334
The announcement mentions governance, but I don't want to assume a corporate change lets one company set the project's direction.
公告提到了治理，但我不想因此就认为企业层面的变动能让一家公司决定项目方向。

32
00:03:14,334 --> 00:03:24,303
Brian: The article says Ray joined the PyTorch Foundation in October 2025, and it describes Ray's governance as being under the Foundation since then.
Brian：文章称 Ray 于 2025 年 10 月加入 PyTorch 基金会，此后一直由基金会负责治理。

33
00:03:24,303 --> 00:03:30,298
It also calls the Foundation a vendor-neutral, community-driven home for its projects.
文章还称基金会为旗下项目提供厂商中立、社区驱动的归属平台。

34
00:03:30,298 --> 00:03:35,038
Nscale's commitment is to keep investing in Ray within that setting.
Nscale 承诺在这一框架下继续投资 Ray。

35
00:03:35,038 --> 00:03:38,804
It doesn't describe a change to Ray's governance.
公告没有提到 Ray 的治理会改变。

36
00:03:38,804 --> 00:03:42,028
Ava: So there are two kinds of commitment to track.
Ava：所以有两种承诺需要关注。

37
00:03:42,028 --> 00:03:46,935
One is Nscale saying it'll support Ray's development and contributors.
一是 Nscale 表示将支持 Ray 的开发和贡献者。

38
00:03:46,935 --> 00:03:51,421
The other is becoming a Platinum member of the wider Foundation.
二是成为整个基金会的白金会员。

39
00:03:51,421 --> 00:03:55,135
Those are related, but they aren't the same decision.
两者有关联，但属于不同的决定。

40
00:03:55,135 --> 00:04:02,074
The first concerns a project; the second gives Nscale a formal place in Foundation governance.
前者涉及一个项目；后者让 Nscale 正式参与基金会治理。

41
00:04:02,074 --> 00:04:05,685
Brian: Nick Jones explains the motivation from Nscale's side.
Brian：Nick Jones 解释了 Nscale 的动机。

42
00:04:05,685 --> 00:04:14,444
He says infrastructure providers often treat the framework and data center as separate problems, while Nscale treats them together.
他说，基础设施提供商往往把框架和数据中心视为两个独立的问题，而 Nscale 把它们放在一起考虑。

43
00:04:14,444 --> 00:04:24,288
His point is that a company building the infrastructure underneath PyTorch and Ray should also support the open-source ecosystem it relies on.
他的意思是，建设 PyTorch 和 Ray 底层基础设施的公司，也应该支持自己所依赖的开源生态。

44
00:04:24,288 --> 00:04:27,125
Ava: I can follow that as an engineering goal.
Ava：作为工程目标，这一点我能理解。

45
00:04:27,125 --> 00:04:34,183
Nick is saying the framework, distributed layer, and physical cloud shouldn't be treated in isolation.
Nick 的意思是，框架、分布式层和实体云基础设施不该孤立看待。

46
00:04:34,183 --> 00:04:39,650
Mark Collier, the Foundation's executive director, also emphasizes integration.
基金会执行董事 Mark Collier 也强调了整合。

47
00:04:39,650 --> 00:04:46,574
What scale of workload does he have in mind, and what does he want that integration to improve?
他考虑的工作负载有多大？希望这种整合改善什么？

48
00:04:46,574 --> 00:04:51,893
Brian: He points to frontier AI workloads that scale to multi-trillion parameters.
Brian：他提到参数规模达数万亿的前沿 AI 工作负载。

49
00:04:51,893 --> 00:04:59,553
He says integration among PyTorch, distributed frameworks like Ray, and cluster infrastructure is essential.
他说，PyTorch、Ray 等分布式框架与集群基础设施之间的整合至关重要。

50
00:04:59,553 --> 00:05:05,227
He names less friction for developers and better multi-node performance as aims.
他的目标包括减少开发者遇到的阻力，提升多节点性能。

51
00:05:05,227 --> 00:05:12,244
Those are goals in his welcome statement, rather than results we can attach to a specific run.
这些是他在欢迎辞中提出的目标，而非某次具体运行已取得的成果。

52
00:05:12,244 --> 00:05:15,893
Ava: That gives us a useful way to read the announcement.
Ava：这为我们解读公告提供了一个有用的角度。

53
00:05:15,893 --> 00:05:21,227
Nscale is deciding to support the ecosystem and take part in its governance.
Nscale决定支持这个生态系统，并参与其治理。

54
00:05:21,227 --> 00:05:29,087
For a team planning a distributed run, the design still depends on its own workload and technical documentation.
对计划开展分布式运行的团队来说，具体设计仍取决于自身负载和技术文档。

55
00:05:29,087 --> 00:05:34,770
So what does Platinum membership formally give Nscale inside the Foundation?
那么，白金会员资格正式赋予Nscale在基金会内哪些权利？

56
00:05:34,770 --> 00:05:39,030
Brian: It grants 1 seat on the PyTorch Foundation Governing Board.
Brian：它让Nscale在PyTorch基金会治理委员会获得1个席位。

57
00:05:39,030 --> 00:05:45,240
The Board sets policy through the Foundation's bylaws, mission, and vision statements.
治理委员会依据基金会章程、使命和愿景声明制定政策。

58
00:05:45,240 --> 00:05:51,667
Those describe the broad scope of its initiatives and its technical vision and direction.
这些文件界定了基金会各项计划的总体范围，以及技术愿景和方向。

59
00:05:51,667 --> 00:05:54,267
Nick Jones is welcomed to that seat.
Nick Jones将出任这一席位。

60
00:05:54,267 --> 00:05:59,888
It's a defined way for Nscale to take part in Foundation-level decisions.
这为Nscale参与基金会层面的决策提供了明确途径。

61
00:05:59,888 --> 00:06:06,357
Ava: A seat gives a voice, but the article doesn't say that one member controls technical decisions.
Ava：席位意味着有发言权，但文章并未说单个成员能主导技术决策。

62
00:06:06,357 --> 00:06:11,056
Nick's current job is close to the infrastructure part of this story.
Nick目前的工作与这里涉及的基础设施密切相关。

63
00:06:11,056 --> 00:06:15,823
He leads engineering strategy for Nscale's high-performance GPU cloud.
他负责Nscale高性能GPU云的工程战略。

64
00:06:15,823 --> 00:06:22,438
That makes his appointment easy to connect to the company's stated focus on the whole stack.
因此，他的任命与公司宣称的全技术栈重点很容易联系起来。

65
00:06:22,438 --> 00:06:31,466
Brian: The article says Nick brings more than 15 years of experience across cloud-native infrastructure, AI, and high-performance computing.
Brian：文章称，Nick在云原生基础设施、AI和高性能计算领域拥有超过15年经验。

66
00:06:31,466 --> 00:06:41,445
It also mentions his work on large-scale GPU cloud platforms and contributions to projects spanning Kubernetes, OpenStack, and distributed systems.
文章还提到，他曾参与大型GPU云平台建设，并为涉及Kubernetes、OpenStack和分布式系统的项目作出贡献。

67
00:06:41,445 --> 00:06:48,108
Those background details help explain the infrastructure expertise the Foundation highlights.
这些经历说明了基金会所强调的基础设施专长。

68
00:06:48,108 --> 00:06:50,458
Ava: There's another appointment too.
Ava：还有另一项任命。

69
00:06:50,458 --> 00:06:59,124
Eyal Lantzman, Nscale's vice president of AI services, is joining the Foundation's Technical Advisory Council, or TAC.
Nscale的AI服务副总裁Eyal Lantzman将加入基金会技术咨询委员会（TAC）。

70
00:06:59,124 --> 00:07:04,412
His area sounds closer to serving models than to operating data centers.
他的工作似乎更偏向模型服务，而非数据中心运营。

71
00:07:04,412 --> 00:07:10,490
What does the article tell us about his work, beyond the title of the council?
除了委员会职务，文章还介绍了他的哪些工作？

72
00:07:10,490 --> 00:07:18,911
Brian: At Nscale, Eyal leads the AI services stack, focused on serving and optimizing large open-weight models in production.
Brian：在Nscale，Eyal负责AI服务技术栈，重点是在生产环境中提供开放权重的大模型服务并优化这些模型。

73
00:07:18,911 --> 00:07:28,118
He brings more than 20 years of experience across AI and machine learning platforms, cloud infrastructure, and developer tooling.
他在AI与机器学习平台、云基础设施及开发者工具领域拥有超过20年经验。

74
00:07:28,118 --> 00:07:35,176
The article also notes his long-standing focus on cloud security, governance, and sovereignty.
文章还提到，他长期关注云安全、治理和主权。

75
00:07:35,176 --> 00:07:40,674
Ava: We can separate those claims. His serving focus describes his role at Nscale.
Ava：这两点可以分开看。他对模型服务的关注描述的是他在Nscale的职责。

76
00:07:40,674 --> 00:07:45,671
His TAC appointment describes how he'll participate in the Foundation.
他获任TAC委员，则说明他将如何参与基金会工作。

77
00:07:45,671 --> 00:07:52,454
The announcement doesn't name a TAC project for him or define a technical change he'll deliver.
公告没有指定他负责的TAC项目，也没有说明他将交付什么技术改进。

78
00:07:52,454 --> 00:07:58,230
That distinction matters when we read a personnel announcement as engineers.
工程师解读人事任命公告时，需要分清这一点。

79
00:07:58,230 --> 00:08:02,305
Brian: The Foundation itself covers more than one project.
Brian：基金会支持的不止一个项目。

80
00:08:02,305 --> 00:08:08,778
It supports core PyTorch alongside Ray, vLLM, DeepSpeed, Helion, and Safetensors.
除了PyTorch核心项目，它还支持Ray、vLLM、DeepSpeed、Helion和Safetensors。

81
00:08:08,778 --> 00:08:14,771
It's a vendor-neutral, community-driven hub hosted by the Linux Foundation.
它是由Linux基金会托管、厂商中立且由社区驱动的平台。

82
00:08:14,771 --> 00:08:23,482
The article describes its scope as training, optimizing, serving, and running models across chips and clouds.
文章称，其工作范围涵盖跨芯片和云环境的模型训练、优化、服务和运行。

83
00:08:23,482 --> 00:08:27,188
Nscale has joined that wider organization.
Nscale加入的是这个更广泛的组织。

84
00:08:27,188 --> 00:08:28,974
Ava: That portfolio is broad.
Ava：这个项目组合覆盖面很广。

85
00:08:28,974 --> 00:08:36,863
If I work on model serving, I might notice vLLM and Safetensors in the same Foundation as PyTorch and Ray.
如果我从事模型服务，可能会注意到vLLM和Safetensors与PyTorch、Ray同属一个基金会。

86
00:08:36,863 --> 00:08:42,817
But the membership announcement has one specific project commitment from Nscale.
但这份入会公告中，Nscale只对一个具体项目作出了承诺。

87
00:08:42,817 --> 00:08:50,386
Is it fair to say that commitment is about Ray, while the Platinum membership is Foundation-wide?
可以说，这项承诺针对Ray，而白金会员资格涵盖整个基金会吗？

88
00:08:50,386 --> 00:08:50,660
Brian: Yes.
Brian：可以。

89
00:08:50,660 --> 00:08:56,554
Nscale commits to continued investment in Ray's development and contributor community.
Nscale承诺继续投入Ray的开发及其贡献者社区。

90
00:08:56,554 --> 00:09:02,448
The Platinum seat belongs to the Foundation's Governing Board, whose remit is broader.
白金会员席位属于基金会治理委员会，其职责范围更广。

91
00:09:02,448 --> 00:09:08,274
The article doesn't assign Nscale a separate plan for every project in the portfolio.
文章没有为Nscale列出针对项目组合中每个项目的单独计划。

92
00:09:08,274 --> 00:09:16,848
That distinction helps us understand the scope of the promise without reading extra commitments into a list of projects.
分清这一点，才能准确理解承诺的范围，避免从项目清单中推断出额外承诺。

93
00:09:16,848 --> 00:09:20,207
Ava: Here's the takeaway for a framework engineer.
Ava：对框架工程师来说，关键是这几点。

94
00:09:20,207 --> 00:09:25,432
Nscale first came into the Foundation's project ecosystem through Ray.
Nscale最初是通过Ray进入基金会项目生态的。

95
00:09:25,432 --> 00:09:32,598
Its acquisition of Anyscale is planned, and its commitment to keep supporting Ray is stated now.
收购Anyscale仍处于计划阶段，而Nscale现已明确承诺继续支持Ray。

96
00:09:32,598 --> 00:09:40,286
Nscale has also joined as a Platinum member, with Nick Jones on the Board and Eyal Lantzman on the TAC.
Nscale也已成为白金会员，Nick Jones进入治理委员会，Eyal Lantzman加入TAC。

97
00:09:40,286 --> 00:09:42,950
Those are the concrete changes.
这些是已经明确的变化。

98
00:09:42,950 --> 00:09:52,895
Brian: Keep the timeline straight: Ray has been under Foundation governance since October 2025, while the Anyscale acquisition is still planned.
Brian：要理清时间线：Ray自2025年10月起由基金会治理，而收购Anyscale仍处于计划阶段。

99
00:09:52,895 --> 00:10:03,203
Keep the engineering layers clear too: PyTorch is the framework, Ray supports distributed computing, and Nscale provides cloud infrastructure.
也要分清技术层次：PyTorch是框架，Ray支持分布式计算，Nscale提供云基础设施。

100
00:10:03,203 --> 00:10:10,970
The stated goal is smoother work across those layers, backed by membership and continued investment in Ray.
其既定目标是让这些层次之间的协作更顺畅，白金会员资格和对Ray的持续投入为此提供支持。

101
00:10:10,970 --> 00:10:12,844
Thanks for listening.
感谢收听。
